<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93339" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάρκ-ῐνος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>like flesh, fleshy</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ὄζος</span> (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄζος</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ς. [μέρη</span>]
				<i>fleshy</i> parts, such as the gums, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				493a1
			</span></i>; <i>made of flesh</i> (and blood), <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>EN</u>
				1117b5
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθρωποι θνατοὶ καὶ ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hipparch.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.44.81
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>D.</u>
				3
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sign.</u>
				34
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ἰχθῦς</span> (opp. a dream)
				<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				21.66
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς τὸ χρήσιμον καὶ ς. καὶ
				ὠφέλιμον [ἔχουσι τῶν λόγων</span>]
			<i>substantial</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.79c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>made of gut</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχοινία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PLond.</u>
					3.1177.169
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>fleshly, of the flesh, Ep. Hebr.</i><i><span class="en">
				7.16
			</span></i>, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Rom.</u>
				7.14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>fleshy, corpulent</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				711
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				387
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σώματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					906c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάρκινος ἤτοι γυργαθός</span>, perh. 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαργάνη</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Edict.Diocl.</u>
				32.18
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
